    {
      "port": 5432,
      "title": "Docker publishes port 5432 (lab-db) past the firewall",
      "cause": "Docker publishes this port past the firewall. Docker's NAT rules send the traffic to the container before UFW's INPUT rules see it, so `ufw deny 5432` never applies.",
      "location": {
        "file": "/home/user/lab-host-slice/docker-compose.yml",
        "line": 18,
        "text": "- \"5432:5432\""
      },
      "fix": "At /home/user/lab-host-slice/docker-compose.yml:18 change\n    - \"5432:5432\"\nto\n    - \"127.0.0.1:5432:5432\"\nthen run\n    docker compose -p lab-host-slice -f /home/user/lab-host-slice/docker-compose.yml up -d lab-db\nIf other machines must reach it, keep it published and restrict it in the DOCKER-USER iptables chain instead (not automated here).",
      "undo": "Put the original line back (- \"5432:5432\") and run the same command:\n    docker compose -p lab-host-slice -f /home/user/lab-host-slice/docker-compose.yml up -d lab-db",
      "lockout": "This cuts off every client that reaches lab-db on 203.0.113.71:5432 from another machine (apps on other servers, your own database client). It does not touch SSH. Recreating the container restarts lab-db briefly."
